{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{# Specific context for the brief summary of Section 8 (User Interaction) #}
{% set output_format_description = "a single, concise sentence (maximum 2 sentences) summarizing the main conclusion about user interaction requirements from this section" %}

{% block task_instructions %}
Read the generated narrative, chart insight, and callout provided below for "{{ section_title }}", which focuses on user interaction requirements.
Distill this information down to the single most important takeaway message about the role of user interaction in exploits during this period.
Your output must be extremely concise: just one sentence, or two at the absolute maximum.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Section Key: {{ data_context_payload.section_key | default('section_8_user_interaction_deep_dive') }}

Generated Narrative for this Section:
{{ data_context_payload.generated_narrative | default("Narrative not available.") }}

Chart Insights Generated for this Section:
{% for chart_id, insight in data_context_payload.chart_insights_in_section.items() %}
- Insight ({{ chart_id }}): {{ insight }}
{% else %}
- No specific chart insights provided.
{% endfor %}

Callouts Generated for this Section:
{% for callout_key, callout_text in data_context_payload.callouts_in_section.items() %}
- {{ callout_key | replace("_", " ") | title }}: {{ callout_text }}
{% else %}
- No callouts generated for this section.
{% endfor %}
{% endblock data_context %}
